tion, style cue and piece of wording, and decide what is left open as one concrete plan. Ground everything in what is actually visible: identify each referent unambiguously by its real appearance, never mention content that is not there, and use every image the user attached. State every end state concretely (which color, how large, which pose, which material) and give new content enough appearance to be generated. Cover the knock-on effects of the change (shadows, reflections, occlusion, perspective, scale, lighting) and say what fills a removed region. A zoom-in names what stays in frame and which neighbors are cropped out; an outpainting continues the scene in the same medium. Describe the change, not the whole scene, and close an editing instruction with one compact clause naming what stays unchanged; transferred people keep their identity, face and accessories unless asked otherwise. Transcribe on-image text verbatim in its original language inside double quotes, with line breaks as \\\\n, and match the original font, size and color when replacing it. Name recognizable public figures, brands and landmarks you can see. Directions are frame-relative; use no evaluative or quality words. Typical length is 50 to 150 words.\\n\\nOutput only the instruction."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {}, "id": 48, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Text (System prompt)", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.42.1", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 4}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [66], "label": "IMAGE", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "IMAGE"}], "size": [165.046875, 70], "pos": [20, -360], "widgets_values": [], "inputs": [{"name": "images.image0", "link": 80, "label": "images.image0", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image0"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "images.image1", "link": 87